Package: lufux
Version: 1.3.9
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Mikhail Mlhcnn <mikhail@advnirr.org>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Advnirr/lufux
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.10), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), wimtools, rsync, parted, pkexec | policykit-1, dosfstools, ntfs-3g
Recommends: udisks2
Suggests: grub2-common, grub-pc-bin
Description: Create bootable USB drives, including Windows To Go
 A GTK4/libadwaita tool that writes ISOHybrid images with dd, builds Windows
 installation media (GPT/FAT32 for UEFI, MBR/NTFS for Legacy BIOS) and
 installs Windows To Go onto a USB drive.
 .
 udisks2 lets it read the edition list out of a Windows ISO without a
 password. grub2-common and grub-pc-bin are needed only for MBR media.
